FINALLY! After so many games, I got this one. I mean I've been to the
endgame many many times, and into gehennom even more, but it was just
at the end which I got stuck. As almost always I played an elven
wizard.

This time I took it slow. I only played as long as I was enjoying it
(when I got into frustrated stubbornness YASD was not long after). Did
it bit by bit. When I got into problems I didn't panic, but grinned
and went "great a problem! Let's see how I can solve this!" (Amazing
how many life lessons I've learnt from ol' nethack)

So the early game was good. I raided a huge ring shop, managed to
write a spellbook of identify, and was early on thereby equipped to
deal with anything a ring can solve. I never used conflict much in my
previous games, but I finally got the trick of it this time, and it
certainly saved me on the planes.

Both magic markers and wishes of all sorts were amazingly plentiful in
this game. There was a miserable minetown (only Izchack) but as if as
a compensation I got a /oWishing in a death drop right in the middle
of his store. As I play chaotic I usually wish for the master key of
thievery, but that waited till the wand at the castle. I didn't
sacrifice (played all through with a +7 quarterstaff) and luckily
there were no randomly generated artifacts to spoil that wish.

I found a succubus in a no teleport level in gehennom and blocked the
passage with boulders, simply leaning on the wait key and watching the
levels build up. I got killed once by not noticing some demons that
flew over, but I just wished for another amulet of life saving and
continued.

When I could I genocided ;, L, h, and P (I love purple worm pets, and
they eat green slimes).

Rodney was nothing: I always killed him first turn with Finger of
Death. Coming back up, though, I hit a problem. My unicorn horn got
cursed so I wielded it, forgetting it was a weapon, to cast remove
curse. My hands stuck to it, so I couldn't cast, couldn't get holy
water out of my bag, etc. A tricky situation. So... I basically had to
hack my way oh so slowly through the levels sitting on every magic
trap I could find. My armour was too good for the monsters, but was it
slow. I got it on maybe the 6th trap. Phew.

The elementals were easy. Astral was tougher, the only level I had
almost no experience of, but I was well prepared, created an army of
purple worms and slogged through, using them as a barrier if nothing
else when I wanted to escape the riders. The second _ I checked was
it. For a few seconds I just couldn't f-ing believe it.

Oh man that was sweet. Now I've deleted Nethack and won't play again
until I have made myself some financial freedom in the Real World.
Sooo much time wasted. But I'm glad it was Nethack and not Facebook or
something, anyway.


